Cyberphone
Modifications Copyright (c) 2026 Yshawn6720

Cyberphone is a modified version (fork) of FFXIV-Aetherphone, based on
upstream tag v1.3.3.0 (commit 4b72228612b0616a41640fc3c846114f5104ab00,
https://github.com/XeldarAlz/FFXIV-Aetherphone). It is not Aetherphone, is not
endorsed by its authors, and does not connect to the official Aethernet
servers. Report problems to https://github.com/Yshawn6720/Cyberphone, not to
the Aetherphone project. The modified version is licensed under the same
terms, AGPL-3.0-or-later.

Modifications (AGPL-3.0 section 5(a)), first made 2026-10-21:

- 2026-10-21  Ported to the Traditional Chinese client's Dalamud (API 13,
              .NET 9): SDK downgrade, Dalamud/Lumina/ClientStructs API
              differences, net9 test project.
- 2026-10-21  Official Aethernet hosts blocked before DNS resolution by
              src/Aetherphone/Core/Net/OfficialHostGuard.cs, the only place
              that creates HTTP clients and WebSockets; default service base
              URL points at a reserved .invalid name. Guarded by
              src/Aetherphone.Tests/OfflineGuaranteeTests.cs.
- 2026-10-21  Aethernet-only apps (social, chat, calls, casino, coin,
              feedback, polls, Muster, Yellow Pages), Strats and announcements
              hidden; account sign-in removed from setup and Settings; links
              to upstream community and donation pages removed.
- 2026-10-21  Renamed to Cyberphone in player-visible text (all nine
              languages), slash commands /cyberphone and /cphone, plugin
              manifest, plugin file Cyberphone.dll and InternalName
              Cyberphone. The assembly name and code namespaces remain
              "Aetherphone" for now because the bundled SixLabors licence is
              scoped to that assembly name.
- 2026-10-21  App icons, plugin icon and emblem regenerated from Phosphor
              Icons (MIT) duotone glyphs in Cyberphone's own style; seasonal
              icon variants dropped.
- 2026-10-21  Removed assets that need their owners' permission: the 58
              contributed artwork phone cases (src/Aetherphone/Cases/*.png)
              and the Rolladeck partner mark (Icons/rolladeck.png).
- 2026-10-21  Added a Traditional Chinese (Taiwan) language with Taiwan
              client language detection; the shared CJK font now draws the
              game's own Axis glyphs; Hunts is hidden on the Traditional
              Chinese client, which Faloop does not serve; realtime signals
              are no longer sent while Aethernet is off.
- 2026-10-21  Watch parties run through a self-hosted relay instead of
              Aethernet: relay server in server/ (Cloudflare Worker and
              Durable Objects, see docs/self-hosting-relay.md); MogCast
              settings for the relay address and invite code; the party tab
              appears only when both are set, and the plugin connects only
              when a party is started or joined. Host heartbeat relaxed from
              8 to 30 seconds. Party features the relay does not implement
              are hidden while using it.
- 2026-10-22  The in-world video screen is drawn from Dalamud's UI draw
              callback instead of a DirectX Present hook, so turning the
              plugin off and on leaves no hook behind in the game's present
              call; the screen now hides whenever Dalamud hides plugin
              windows. ScreenPainter logs why a frame was not drawn, only
              when the reason changes.
- 2026-10-22  Music Jam runs through the same self-hosted relay: a JamRoom
              Durable Object in server/, the shared relay address and invite
              code from MogCast settings, and a connection only while a Jam
              is started or joined. Host heartbeat relaxed from 8 to 30
              seconds; the relay ends the Jam when the host leaves.
- 2026-10-22  The MogCast relay party regains join approval, queue
              suggestions, reactions and removing a member. The relay holds
              newcomers until the host approves, passes suggestions to the
              host and the answer back to the author, forwards reactions on
              a separate per-member budget (the plugin sends at most 4 at
              once, then 1 a second) and closes a removed member's
              connection; the plugin does not reconnect after being removed
              or declined. Nearby parties stay unavailable.
- 2026-10-22  Announcements and the in-game events in Calendar come back
              through the self-hosted relay: server/content holds both as
              static JSON that the Worker serves behind the invite code, with
              an ETag and no Durable Object. The plugin keeps a local copy,
              checks again at most every 6 hours and only when Announcements
              or Calendar is shown, sends no announcement notifications, and
              keeps Announcements hidden with no request while no relay is
              set.
- 2026-10-22  Games "Play together" comes back through the self-hosted relay
              as invite-based rooms: a GameRoom Durable Object in server/
              referees Uno, Chess, Connect Four and Broadside itself, keeps
              hands and fleets private, and closes the room when the host
              leaves. The plugin connects only while a room is created or
              joined, sends one move at a time under its own budget, and
              hides 8-Ball Pool, Moogle War, Mini Golf, Lucky Draw, the
              public room list, matchmaking and leaderboards while on the
              relay.
- 2026-10-22  Voice calls come back as invite-based call rooms in a new
              Calls tab in Linkpearl: a CallRoom Durable Object in server/
              forwards Opus frames between up to 4 members without decoding
              or storing them, and only runs where CALLS_ENABLED is on (the
              Docker compose setup; the Workers configuration keeps it off
              and answers 403). The plugin connects only while a room is
              open, closes the link as soon as the call is left, never
              retries a server without calls, and keeps direct dialing,
              ringing, the online list, the Control Center toggle, Spotlight
              and the call command hidden.
- 2026-10-22  MogCast fullscreen covers the game viewport in its own window
              with fit and fill modes, a volume slider and controls that fade
              when idle; the phone is not drawn while fullscreen. The screen
              page gains Big Screen, which places a flat in-world screen in
              front of the camera at 85 percent of the view. The landscape
              theater mode is removed.
- 2026-10-22  The assembly is renamed to Cyberphone with Cyberphone's own
              SixLabors community licence; code namespaces stay
              "Aetherphone". Legacy settings type names now migrate to the
              Cyberphone assembly.
- 2026-10-22  Music Jam on the relay regains join approval, guest
              permissions, reactions and removing a member, and a removed
              guest no longer reconnects. Watch parties and Jams can be
              found nearby again: a host opts in per room (off by default),
              and the relay's GET /rooms/nearby lists only those rooms in the
              asker's territory and world, under a separate nearby code and
              the host's character name, rate limited per address. Tapping a
              listed room sends a join request that always waits for the
              host's approval. A viewer's failed playback is reported to the
              host only.
- 2026-10-22  The Traditional Chinese client gets its own news through the
              self-hosted relay: server/scripts/fetch-tw-news.mjs reads the
              news lists of www.ffxiv.com.tw and keeps only titles, dates,
              categories, links, a short summary and maintenance windows in
              server/content/news-tw.json, which the Worker serves as
              /content/news-tw behind the invite code with an ETag. News on
              that client reads only this document, shows nothing instead of
              North American Lodestone news while no relay is set, has no
              Status tab, and checks again at most every 6 hours and only
              while News is shown; the home widget reads the local copy only.
              Lodestone portraits and lookups are off on that client, as on
              the Chinese one.
- 2026-10-22  Music Radio shows a curated station list from the relay's
              /content/radio (server/content/radio.json: name, stream URL,
              genre, homepage) in place of the community radio, only while a
              relay is set and the Radio page is shown, cached for 6 hours.
              The MogCast info page describes the relay watch party: invites,
              and approving or denying who joins.
- 2026-10-23  A relay watch party is listed nearby only when the host's
              state carries nearbyOptIn beside discoverable, so hosts on
              1.3.4.0 and earlier, which send discoverable by default, stay
              unlisted. When the relay answers 404 for news, curated stations
              or the nearby list, those pages say the relay does not support
              the feature yet instead of reporting a connection failure.
- 2026-10-23  A watch party viewer whose player ends the video early, as
              mpv does when a download drops, reopens the host's link at the
              host's position while the host still plays it, instead of
              staying stopped until the viewer leaves and rejoins.
- 2026-10-23  When a link's download drops more than 10 seconds before the
              video's end, which mpv reports as the end of the file, MogCast
              restarts the link where it stopped, on the stall watchdog's
              restart budget, instead of counting the video as finished and
              moving the queue (and a watch party) on to the next video.
- 2026-10-23  The relay watch party forwards danmaku: a member's
              stream.danmaku line is cleaned of control, format and
              private-use characters, cut to 60 code points and sent on as
              stream.danmakuLine with the sender's id stamped by the relay, on
              its own rate bucket. The host's state can switch danmaku off for
              the room, the relay keeps no copy of any line, and features
              gains bit 2 so older plugins and relays keep working.
- 2026-10-23  Watch party members can send danmaku from a composer under the
              reaction bar. Lines are cleaned again on arrival,
              scroll right to left across the top of the video on the world
              screen, the full screen window and the phone player, in 1 to 5
              rows (3 by default), with the sender's name in front and an
              outline on your own. Each player can turn danmaku off or hide one
              member for the party, the host can turn it off for the room, and
              the composer only appears when the relay reports the feature.
- 2026-10-23  While a watch party host's player restarts a link after a
              stall, a refused stream or a dropped download, the host keeps
              publishing the position it projected for that link until the
              link loads again, instead of the restarting player's position 0,
              which sent the viewers back to the start of the video.
- 2026-10-23  The watch party host also keeps publishing its projected
              position for the same link while mpv has no position to report:
              in the moment between mpv ending the file and the restart
              starting, and while the host reloads the same link. A restart
              that began in that moment no longer sends the viewers back to
              the start either.
- 2026-10-23  /cyberphone dm <text> (and /cphone dm) sends a watch party
              danmaku line from the game's chat box through the composer's
              path, and prints why in chat when it cannot: empty text, not in
              a party, not connected, a relay without danmaku, the host
              turned it off, or sending too fast. Your own lines are drawn
              like everyone else's, without the outline.
- 2026-10-23  A watch party join from the nearby list follows the host's
              Require approval to join, like a join with the invite: with
              approval off it enters at once, and turning approval off
              mid-party lets everyone waiting in. The relay applies this only
              while the current host's state carries nearbyFollowsApproval,
              so hosts on 1.3.6.0 and earlier, whose settings say such a join
              always waits, keep holding it for approval. Jam joins from the
              nearby list still always wait.
- 2026-10-23  With both MogCast screens playing, the Watch page shows a Sound
              row (Screen A, Screen B, Both) above the Screen B card. Only the
              picked screen is heard, so picking the other one moves the
              sound in one tap; Both plays the two together, each with its own
              volume and a speaker that mutes it. A screen that fails or
              stops hands the sound to the other until it plays again. Sound
              fading with distance no longer decides which screen is heard,
              and the main screen choice left the Screen page.
- 2026-10-23  Screen B is easier to reach: while it is empty and screen A has
              a video, the Watch page shows Play on Screen B, which opens the
              add sheet with Screen B picked, and queue and history rows offer
              the same action, keeping the title and thumbnail (a queue entry
              leaves the queue, a history entry resumes where it stopped).
              Viewers do not see these entries. While both screens are up,
              Side by Side and Stacked under Big Screen join A and B edge to
              edge in front of the camera as one flat wall, A on the left or
              top.
- 2026-10-23  The Watch page gets Screen A and Screen B tabs at the top, each
              captioned with what that screen is doing and lit while it is
              heard. The picked tab runs one player layout for that screen:
              progress and seek, time, play and pause, 10 second skips,
              volume and mute, Screen Placement and Stop; an empty B tab
              starts a video on B. This replaces the Screen B card and the
              Play on Screen B button. Each screen now keeps its own volume
              and mute whichever screen is heard, tapping the speaker of a
              silent screen moves the sound to it, and danmaku typed on a
              tab goes to that tab's screen.
- 2026-10-23  A MogCast live stream starts at its live edge instead of about
              an hour behind: a play from the top sends mpv no start
              position, and a live link drops any start position it was
              opened with (a resume, a viewer joining, a restart), which used
              to land past the end and show no picture. In a watch party, a
              viewer of a live stream no longer follows the host's position
              (each member's live clock differs), only the link, pause and
              screen, and reopens the stream at the live edge when it ends
              while the host still shows it.
- 2026-10-23  A watch party viewer whose seeks take longer than the sync
              tolerance catches up instead of seeking forever: a follow-up
              seek aims ahead by the time the last one took, and when two
              seeks in a row have not closed the gap the viewer reopens the
              link at the host's position instead of a third, at most once a
              minute. A viewer no longer seeks while its own player restarts
              a link or has no position.
- 2026-10-23  A MogCast link whose seek or buffering has not finished after
              30 seconds restarts at that position, under the same restart
              budget as other stalls, instead of waiting without end or log.
- 2026-10-23  A watch party outlives its host's dropped connection by 60
              seconds instead of ending at once: the relay keeps the room,
              tells viewers the host is reconnecting with a countdown, and
              hands the room back (code, members, pending join requests)
              when the host's plugin reconnects with its room code, which it
              now tries up to 3 times. Leaving on purpose still ends the room
              at once. The plugin logs why a relay connection closed and how
              long it lasted, and the relay logs when a host drops, returns
              or a room ends, with the reason.
- 2026-10-23  A watch party host's plugin tries up to 6 reconnects instead of
              3, so its retries span the relay's 60 second grace.

